<title>GREECE: Greek 1M ATHIBOR rises to 11.84 from 11.63 pct.</title>
<headline>Greek 1M ATHIBOR rises to 11.84 from 11.63 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Athens Interbank Offered Rate (Athibor) rose to 11.84 from 11.63 percent and the bid rate (Athibid) for one month firmed to 11.34 from 11.13 percent.</p>
<p>ATHIBOR</p>
<p> DATE     1-MTH   2-MTH   3-MTH   6-MTH   9-MTH   12-MTH</p>
<p> Aug  05  11.84   11.53   11.41   11.26   11.14   11.04</p>
<p> Aug  04  11.63   11.34   11.21   11.04   10.94   10.91</p>
<p> Aug  01  11.53   11.25   11.20   11.04   11.00   11.00</p>
<p> July 31  11.53   11.22   11.14   11.02   10.96   10.97</p>
<p> July 30  11.79   11.54   11.46   11.23   11.16   11.12</p>
<p> July 29  11.96   11.85   11.70   11.33   11.26   11.18</p>
<p> July 28  11.92   11.84   11.75   11.38   11.32   11.23</p>
<p> July 25  11.91   11.85   11.74   11.46   11.35   11.27</p>
<p>ATHIBID</p>
<p> Aug  05  11.34   11.02   10.90   10.75   10.60   10.52</p>
<p> Aug  04  11.13   10.83   10.71   10.54   10.45   10.40</p>
<p> Aug  01  11.02   10.75   10.70   10.54   10.50   10.50</p>
<p> July 31  11.02   10.72   10.64   10.52   10.46   10.46</p>
<p> July 30  11.27   11.02   10.94   10.72   10.64   10.59</p>
<p> July 29  11.45   11.34   11.19   10.81   10.73   10.64</p>
<p> July 28  11.42   11.32   11.23   10.85   10.77   10.67</p>
<p> July 25  11.39   11.32   11.21   10.92   10.79   10.71</p>
<p>Note: ATHIBOR is Greece's official reference rate. It comprises 18 leading state and private banks committed to quoting their rates by 0900 GMT every day.</p>
<p>--Angelos Kiosklis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
